[{:db/id "q-350830/field-1/ba8784e66daad439a9545d84e4825eeb005857146e5719539cb0aa3a3b249be1" :answer/id #uuid "06fe1340-759b-586c-837e-bd624a59f9d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5e^4}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350830/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4f2aa46-8db9-554e-a213-55c6023dfb62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350830/field-1/ba8784e66daad439a9545d84e4825eeb005857146e5719539cb0aa3a3b249be1" :answer-field/choices ["q-350830/field-1/ba8784e66daad439a9545d84e4825eeb005857146e5719539cb0aa3a3b249be1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350830" :question/id #uuid "c0191a30-c2e2-52a8-94ee-6284596521e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-350830" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4x}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4a}+\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-4x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/ade58ce56684420fb0f00236af50bbb54f76801fc8870e1cce135cbd51f1b726.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a}) \\\\  & =10(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{4}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350830/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350830"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350845/field-1/76da34018574ef19b374c7939c40a93ff98fe0b6df723e936f1c7f6322009d63" :answer/id #uuid "31fdc5d2-1d35-5fea-9c4b-918153ee0c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350845/field-1/934b3dee3759edd32c85abb57e169954d3aec70c4d22ac89ad728cb27f878fd6" :answer/id #uuid "82fbe0aa-009e-538e-b428-1990e4b27f10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350845/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "254750a4-a236-52f8-94b7-2ada10d7b8d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350845/field-1/76da34018574ef19b374c7939c40a93ff98fe0b6df723e936f1c7f6322009d63" :answer-field/choices ["q-350845/field-1/76da34018574ef19b374c7939c40a93ff98fe0b6df723e936f1c7f6322009d63" "q-350845/field-1/934b3dee3759edd32c85abb57e169954d3aec70c4d22ac89ad728cb27f878fd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350845" :question/id #uuid "7abe7254-179c-5b02-b7ca-239c617b5af3" :question/math-academy-id "q-350845" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3x+2}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3a+2}+\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-3x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/425e55256d2e53db1fce6684e2b7b05e8b487d5107dd4abacb8cf17add287c23.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350845/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350847/field-1/cf997d587c5a4dabdcad7e6f0ed2d988ec0108e104402c4cfc86c4c9a0eaaeda" :answer/id #uuid "9ddc04d1-887b-5b34-8b0a-412f0e41741c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{-7}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350847/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "917aa21b-ff2f-51d7-abda-effc9871c024" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350847/field-1/cf997d587c5a4dabdcad7e6f0ed2d988ec0108e104402c4cfc86c4c9a0eaaeda" :answer-field/choices ["q-350847/field-1/cf997d587c5a4dabdcad7e6f0ed2d988ec0108e104402c4cfc86c4c9a0eaaeda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350847" :question/id #uuid "854f43d5-dc5a-5602-b401-4fa8802d3c1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-350847" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4x-3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4a-3}+\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-7}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-4x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/dd3903454e30d878fee3cd1f58f3942db034fde534e514f99e2c14ddd892a9b3.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350847/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350810/field-1/7e070e2b192a8fd1617b620e0d84b9dda3931d9095cb4cac6b9b7771df99f3d4" :answer/id #uuid "3aeb9ff1-6aef-5f6b-b8e8-0191d058f821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5e^{-9}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350810/field-1/7d3a6d895eb2917ba0a4a22db0988885aa79af312d2c0e9df9a252f4aaed2c41" :answer/id #uuid "a71285fa-f291-5636-98d6-005c3db37412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5e^{-9}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350810/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2899872b-928a-5cd9-be75-01d45bdf6c7f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350810/field-1/7e070e2b192a8fd1617b620e0d84b9dda3931d9095cb4cac6b9b7771df99f3d4" :answer-field/choices ["q-350810/field-1/7e070e2b192a8fd1617b620e0d84b9dda3931d9095cb4cac6b9b7771df99f3d4" "q-350810/field-1/7d3a6d895eb2917ba0a4a22db0988885aa79af312d2c0e9df9a252f4aaed2c41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350810" :question/id #uuid "89d283ba-d227-577d-b377-aac9acea03b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-350810" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-3}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}]}_{a}^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-9}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3{e}^{9}}-\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{3x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/2f4fb9b35e0b68c6155ab9b945d10c36d08d878560e93d34d04e610d1983e50c.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3{e}^{9}}-\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(\\frac{1}{3{e}^{9}}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6{e}^{9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350810/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350810"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152884/selection/f003b95a6c7a22f536ec799844670c061a2d01da9486469d5da5d96020e58645" :answer/id #uuid "81869388-99e1-5279-9e9f-d09619be9037" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152884/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" :answer/id #uuid "343f0df1-4ecc-5075-82fb-85e64eae0b77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152884/selection/30658d088d5b87ec1a64410993944d89cb17d534d10aadc650826eb087f134fe" :answer/id #uuid "9e3b06fa-cd87-591a-b95f-259395ba7412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152884/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "6fc20493-7c3d-5625-8de1-dffe627ee2cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152884/selection/1fa32d814e5eecab5821fb8b048d08aefc4fa068dba15b5e3e94d711561b635f" :answer/id #uuid "35c33afe-4c79-570a-ad4b-1aba78b00479" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152884/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ab81b5-3047-554d-a157-6cbf4f7f74b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152884/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" :answer-field/choices ["q-152884/selection/f003b95a6c7a22f536ec799844670c061a2d01da9486469d5da5d96020e58645" "q-152884/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" "q-152884/selection/30658d088d5b87ec1a64410993944d89cb17d534d10aadc650826eb087f134fe" "q-152884/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" "q-152884/selection/1fa32d814e5eecab5821fb8b048d08aefc4fa068dba15b5e3e94d711561b635f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152884" :question/id #uuid "5fcd2373-835d-58c0-a150-1972239e0d50" :question/math-academy-id "q-152884" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x-1}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{e}^{-2x}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2a}}-{e}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/0064a1c234adc9cf5d28d16696bef8a72384a8cc9f85ecc865c5d4ba36dc0d49.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2e}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2a}}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e}(0-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152884/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0d268f-97f9-5db8-863d-dfc237afa546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152884"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20501/selection/cc9e7a7702ef11400fa2755c615ccb574e1cbe77afd485bc3185d37a83c658c8" :answer/id #uuid "5af18c35-79f7-5e01-b585-b7964212c024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20501/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c2bf7242-1dfb-548a-bc3a-a20d63749525" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20501/selection/04d7f54c9b0db558cb68f468594296b6a79616c9d20ce27ce6a6690e554dacf8" :answer/id #uuid "7c5dcbf9-e43b-5d89-bc98-77878fbe3b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20501/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "2f731fd3-82ae-55a9-8245-731d881d6b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20501/selection/f182bf542effa3458d0fd266ffb369313e1975ba415dc738c60d6b1f39ecd6b6" :answer/id #uuid "35ef47f4-95f4-53a5-9912-c4bf11ac6a31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20501/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e0ff1bb-d49d-5f2a-b53d-b9a7ac2b1026" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20501/selection/f182bf542effa3458d0fd266ffb369313e1975ba415dc738c60d6b1f39ecd6b6" :answer-field/choices ["q-20501/selection/cc9e7a7702ef11400fa2755c615ccb574e1cbe77afd485bc3185d37a83c658c8" "q-20501/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-20501/selection/04d7f54c9b0db558cb68f468594296b6a79616c9d20ce27ce6a6690e554dacf8" "q-20501/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-20501/selection/f182bf542effa3458d0fd266ffb369313e1975ba415dc738c60d6b1f39ecd6b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20501" :question/id #uuid "56801e6d-5cbb-50ba-b004-b5f220ae4a1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20501" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {b}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)}{b}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{-{5}^{-x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{5}^{-x}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{a}}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/5949cbdface45cf103ae5bbd14db5d81917c19f3ef82417216e26d2064ca6bd1.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{a}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20501/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20501"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152877/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "51d484ac-9937-59cc-b38b-8d36b365f700" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152877/selection/518e1a324b5f4439d31b4cd535c2ff871ea44859557677ae65953ab21cd53ca0" :answer/id #uuid "80d868ec-c656-54c7-80ec-4aaf0b9b7b74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152877/selection/f94bac1f081684f67b7d5f723610ae9467e04095a582911b4f8a0f2beade8438" :answer/id #uuid "a320fa96-3dd2-51cd-9a41-771e5ec11a52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152877/selection/79a1b9ff5adea9770c7e2865e9c9bffbd5f516ff2fe222926a28c0a8129359da" :answer/id #uuid "03073303-9350-5466-b303-203ed560db91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152877/selection/b688fe75f5731193539287c1dd3267816d354887c7a427e8c7ffea4fc225840a" :answer/id #uuid "f01235d5-adfa-5808-ad11-8aac14a930d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152877/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb315466-dfca-501c-ac07-0ff5e99cad60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152877/selection/b688fe75f5731193539287c1dd3267816d354887c7a427e8c7ffea4fc225840a" :answer-field/choices ["q-152877/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" "q-152877/selection/518e1a324b5f4439d31b4cd535c2ff871ea44859557677ae65953ab21cd53ca0" "q-152877/selection/f94bac1f081684f67b7d5f723610ae9467e04095a582911b4f8a0f2beade8438" "q-152877/selection/79a1b9ff5adea9770c7e2865e9c9bffbd5f516ff2fe222926a28c0a8129359da" "q-152877/selection/b688fe75f5731193539287c1dd3267816d354887c7a427e8c7ffea4fc225840a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152877" :question/id #uuid "393d72cd-a037-522f-8ffe-6b40d5fb5ab2" :question/math-academy-id "q-152877" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{3}{2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}]}_{a}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{2}^{x}]}_{a}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({2}^{3}-{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={2}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{2}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{2}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/b9a29cbd8a029e0f26e3da6a042ada0f8a809053233979bb4ff73db3dcf0f10d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-152877/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152877"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351417/field-1/67c038c3661b204e3dea441216d41a01fd1b794ac613f167ce4d29d1db61b899" :answer/id #uuid "ba89a20e-ecec-5f2f-974d-efb594302db0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\ln(5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351417/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a136a6e-5687-5056-8d3d-14542c6260d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351417/field-1/67c038c3661b204e3dea441216d41a01fd1b794ac613f167ce4d29d1db61b899" :answer-field/choices ["q-351417/field-1/67c038c3661b204e3dea441216d41a01fd1b794ac613f167ce4d29d1db61b899"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351417" :question/id #uuid "ee1a35ee-9fb2-528c-9b40-05d78a32e70f" :question/math-academy-id "q-351417" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {b}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)}{b}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{5\\cdot {5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{5}^{x}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={5}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{5}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/2fc15149d2097a1965e575e725b4dfb49401c1fe5bb1c5b3e43bf0f4f51743a1.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351417/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351417"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152230/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "d5b6165f-13d7-5d98-8ea6-dc1e93025e15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152230/selection/8d5fbf1904997239bda2119986d845ce25499b8ce809e6a222af96acb4985ba9" :answer/id #uuid "99f3b189-b8e8-5876-8f51-1910936e6078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152230/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d7bf6940-d273-566f-ae3c-97863e5f089b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152230/selection/15aff851ab2807102904f6e00e765d26d734a91dd538d10b770cfeb2fdeede38" :answer/id #uuid "1fb9c396-827e-5b37-a80b-769aab9304e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answ